From: joh@netcom.com (John Oh)
Subject: Intelligence Variations

        Jay Freeman mentioned _The Mismeasure of Man_ by Steven Jay Gould.
 
I bought that book a long time ago but never got around to reading it.  
I'm curious whether Gould says anything in the book about differences in 
intelligence between ethnic groups that are scientifically supported?
 
I suspect not, becuase a couple of years ago in college, one of my roommates 
was taking a course taught jointly by Gould, Robert Nozick, and Alan 
Dershowitz, in which one of the assigned reading pieces was a paper that 
claimed to show significant differences in intelligence among Asians, 
Caucasians, and blacks.  My roommate said that Gould (and maybe the other two) 
believed that scientists should not talk about any differences in intelligence 
even if they exist because once can reasonaAbly expect that such information 
will be misused (I believe that he also attacked the validity of the study).

(BTW, funny coincidence that the name of the course was "Thinking about 
Thinking", same name as a current thread on this list).
 
Anyone have comments about Gould's position regarding the suppression 
of certain types of true information?  It seems that refraining from 
making certain true statements makes sense if one expects that many idiots 
who don't understand statistics will misuse the information, and one judges 
that those negative consequences outweigh any benefit of making the statements.

It seems that if I knew of clear evidence showing differences in intelligence 
among ethnic groups, I wouldn't mind talking about it among a group of 
intelligent friends, but I'd probably decide not to discuss it publicly.
 
BTW, obviously intelligence is not a single well-defined quality, just as 
athleticism is not.  They are various types of mental activity, and one's 
aptitude or ability can vary for each type.  Many types of mental ability 
are surely correlated to different degrees.  What I wonder is whether good 
studies have been done regarding specific types of mental aptitude in various 
ethnic groups.  My understanding is that such studies have been done for 
boys and girls.  Among other things, I heard that boys tend to have more 
aptitude for spatial reasoning than girls, while girls tend to have more 
aptitude for rote memorization.  Any comments about such studies?
 
J oh N


